ress), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but can be grumpy and uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). So reliability good, stress good, but cooperation issues.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), known 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere with crew (cooperation), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (crew), not willing to further education (adaptability). So strong reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication and adaptability concerns.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew), relatively weak leadership (crew), also arrogant may affect communication. So strong technical, responsibility, but crew issues.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Candidate C seems strong on reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A has leadership but unorganized and poor criticism. Candidate D has technical and responsibility but arrogance.\n\nProbably Candidate C is strongest overall despite communication issues? But communication is critical. Egocentric and difficulty communicating could be safety risk. Candidate B's uncooperative also risk. Candidate A's unorganized may affect reliability. Candidate D's arrogance also risk.\n\nWe need to argue. I think Candidate C's reliability and positive crew atmosphere may outweigh communication issues if can be trained. But we need to be cautious. Maybe we should not commit yet, but we need to state a recommendation. Could say I currently lean toward Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nLet's produce message: \"I recommend Candidate C\". Provide evidence: reliability 100%, correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere. Acknowledge concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Explain why still best: strengths in core safety criteria outweigh concerns, and concerns can be mitigated.\n\nProceed."}
